<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manchu-Han dyarchy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as ethnic dyarchy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Manchu-Han dyarchy was the practice in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> of appointing both a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> official to many senior posts. It allowed the Manchu ruling minority to share power with the Han majority while keeping overall control. The system was a key element of Qing governance.</p></div>
